# Backend Rules - Cloud Functions & Cloud Run

## Cloud Functions Standards

### Function Structure

```javascript
import * as functions from "firebase-functions";
import * as admin from "firebase-admin";

const db = admin.firestore();

// Auth trigger: Create student profile on new user
export const onUserCreate = functions.auth.user().onCreate(async (user) => {
  try {
    // 1. Create user document
    await db.collection("users").doc(user.uid).set({
      uid: user.uid,
      email: user.email,
      created_at: admin.firestore.Timestamp.now(),
      last_login: admin.firestore.Timestamp.now(),
    });

    // 2. Create student profile
    const studentRef = db.collection("students").doc();
    await studentRef.set({
      student_id: studentRef.id,
      user_id: user.uid,
      email: user.email,
      created_at: admin.firestore.Timestamp.now(),
      last_active: admin.firestore.Timestamp.now(),
    });

    console.log(`Student created: ${user.uid}`);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(`Error creating student: ${error.message}`);
    // Don't throw - auth is already complete
  }
});

// Firestore trigger: Generate recommendations on goal completion
export const onGoalComplete = functions.firestore
  .document("goals/{goalId}")
  .onUpdate(async (change, context) => {
    const before = change.before.data();
    const after = change.after.data();

    // Only trigger on completion
    if (before.status !== "completed" && after.status === "completed") {
      // Generate recommendations
      console.log(`Goal completed: ${context.params.goalId}`);
    }
  });

// Scheduled: Hourly nudge check
export const checkAndSendNudges = functions.pubsub
  .schedule("every 1 hours")
  .onRun(async (context) => {
    console.log("Nudge check started");
    // Implement nudge logic
    console.log("Nudge check completed");
  });
```

### Error Handling

- **Never throw in auth triggers** - They've already succeeded
- **Log all errors** for debugging
- **Handle partial failures** gracefully
- **Return status** from scheduled functions

```javascript
try {
  // Do work
} catch (error) {
  console.error(`Failed: ${error.message}`);
  // Auth triggers: Don't throw
  // Scheduled: Return error message
  return { error: error.message };
}
```

